.TH KSTAR-TRACE 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-trace \- run a file quietly, then trace machine M on word w
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar trace\fR [options] <file> <machine> <word>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Runs the file without showing its output, then shows every step of
<machine> on <word>, as \fBtrace <machine> on "<word>"\fR would at the end of
the file. <machine> may be any expression, such as \fBto_dfa(r)\fR. Use "" for
the empty word.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<when>\fR
auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR environment variable is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar trace examples/01_dfa.kstar HasDouble1 0110\fR
trace a DFA on 0110
.TP
\fBkstar trace lab.kstar "to_dfa(r)" ""\fR
trace an expression on the empty word
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
